            Asphalt driveway maintenance is four small seasonal jobs, not one big annual project: <strong class="text-white">inspect and clean in spring, seal and protect in summer, prep the surface in fall, and play defense in winter</strong>. Reseal every 2-3 years, fill cracks the week you spot them, and use the right deicer and shovel in winter. Skip the routine and you'll pay for it in potholes; keep it up and a well-built asphalt driveway can easily outlast 20 years.
